USER How do I escape the "${}" in a nix string?
-------
ASSISTANT In Nix, you can escape `${}` in a string by doubling the curly braces. For example:
ASSISTANT 
ASSISTANT ```nix
ASSISTANT "${{not interpolated}}"
ASSISTANT ```
ASSISTANT 
ASSISTANT This will result in the literal string `${not interpolated}`.
ASSISTANT 
ASSISTANT Alternatively, you can use the `''` (indented string) syntax, which does not support interpolation by default:
ASSISTANT 
ASSISTANT ```nix
ASSISTANT ''
ASSISTANT   ${not interpolated}
ASSISTANT ''
ASSISTANT ```
ASSISTANT 
ASSISTANT This will also preserve the `${}` as literal text.
-------
USER What is this command doing: sed '1,/-----BEGIN ENCRYPTED DATA-----/d; /-----END ENCRYPTED DATA-----/,$d' "$ENCRYPTED_DATA_PEM"
USER 
