USER How can I prevent tee from also writing to the standard output?
USER 
USER Reply in English.
LLM RESPONSE 2026-05-20T21:22:21
ASSISTANT To prevent `tee` from writing to standard output, redirect its stdout to `/dev/null`:
ASSISTANT 
ASSISTANT ```bash
ASSISTANT command | tee file > /dev/null
ASSISTANT ```
ASSISTANT 
ASSISTANT This will:
ASSISTANT - Write the output of `command` to `file` (via `tee`).
ASSISTANT - Discard the stdout output (by redirecting to `/dev/null`).
ASSISTANT 
ASSISTANT If you also want to suppress errors, add `2>/dev/null`:
ASSISTANT ```bash
ASSISTANT command | tee file > /dev/null 2>&1
ASSISTANT ```
